    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nI have my setting for width_preview set to a size that is comfortable for viewing a file, but it is much larger than needed for a directory. I would appreciate a width setting that is specifically for viewing files since it is hard to pick a size that works well for both of them.",
